# Architecture rules (V1–V3, V8, V11, V14)

## V1 — OS logic isolation

Platform-specific code lives only under:
- `service/collector/linux/`
- `service/collector/mac/`
- `service/collector/windows/`

Do not add `ProcessBuilder`, `ps`, `systemctl`, `tasklist`, etc. to `InstanceMetricsSender` or `config/`.

## V2 — MetricsCollector contract

Every platform must implement `MetricsCollector`. Use `AbstractMetricsCollector` for shared JMX metrics.

## V3 — Shell in collector layer only

Shell/process execution belongs in collector implementations, not in the orchestration service.

## V8 — Configurable schedules

Use `application.properties` for intervals (`metrics.collection.interval`, `docker.collection.interval`). No hardcoded sleep loops in production code.

## V11 — Graceful degradation

Collector errors return empty collections or log warnings. Never let a single collector failure crash the Spring context or scheduled task.

## V14 — Tests for new collectors

New or changed collector logic requires unit tests in `src/test/java/`.
